    skos:altLabel
        "acclimatation"@en ,
        "acclimation"@en ;
    skos:definition """Processes, including selection and adaptation, by which a population of microorganisms develops the ability to degrade a substance, or develops a tolerance to it.
In experimental systems, allowing an organism to adjust to its environment prior to undertaking a study.
Modification of biological processes or structures in the maintenance of homeostasis in response to change in some environmental quality such as temperature, salinity, light, radiation, or toxicant concentration. Note: It is an expression of phenotypic plasticity of individuals in response to a sublethal change in some environmental factor."""@en ;
    skos:inScheme goldbook: ;
    skos:prefLabel "acclimatisation"@en ;
    skos:topConceptOf goldbook: ;
